  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "So, you've got some home repair projects on your plate and you're not quite sure where to begin. No worries, it's a common spot to be in! First off, you'll want to clearly define what needs to be done. Take some pictures and write down detailed notes about the issue. This helps tremendously when you're talking to potential contractors. Next, it's super important to get a written estimate or contract. Make sure it spells out everything: what labor is included, what materials will be used, and what's *not* included. This avoids any surprises down the road. You should also check that any contractor you consider is licensed and insured – that's a big one for your peace of mind. Don't be afraid to ask for references or to see examples of their past work. It helps you get a feel for their quality and reliability. Lastly, make sure you understand who will actually be doing the work on your property. Knowing these things upfront can save you a lot of headaches. Need a hand sorting it all out? Give HH Remodeling LLC a call; we're happy to walk you through it."
    }
  ],
